WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:04.180 --> 00:00:08.180
You're here for a reason, you're here not for this show ...

00:00:08.300 --> 00:00:10.000
No, no, no, no.

00:00:10.960 --> 00:00:13.500
You're here to learn Swedish.

00:00:13.800 --> 00:00:17.320
I'm here because I love Ingmar Bergman films.

00:00:17.920 --> 00:00:21.520
And after seeing

00:00:21.660 --> 00:00:22.940
all the films

00:00:24.540 --> 00:00:28.740
I thought, well, I have to go and learn the language because it's so ...

00:00:29.280 --> 00:00:34.120
The melody and you know, it's very: «Å, jaha, jaha, jättebra»!

00:00:35.020 --> 00:00:37.020
It's just

00:00:39.520 --> 00:00:44.280
It just made me feel really joyful. It still does!

00:00:44.460 --> 00:00:47.840
And now I'm studying, and I love to study Swedish!

00:00:48.380 --> 00:00:50.360
How long have you been studying now?

00:00:50.680 --> 00:00:52.900
Three weeks now.

00:01:00.580 --> 00:01:03.960
But this weekn

00:01:04.120 --> 00:01:08.040
is the last week.

00:01:08.680 --> 00:01:09.960
You came from jazz.

00:01:10.340 --> 00:01:11.860
Yeah. I still am there.

00:01:12.160 --> 00:01:17.860
Yeah, you're still there. But then you have this, let's call it a detour, to Eurovision Song Contest.

00:01:17.980 --> 00:01:19.720
It's my prostitution!

00:01:20.640 --> 00:01:24.840
You were quite clear about that when when you called it fast food music.

00:01:25.360 --> 00:01:27.010
What do you mean by that?

00:01:27.010 --> 00:01:30.200
You know nowadays, I think maybe I was too

00:01:30.780 --> 00:01:34.300
fundamentalist, you know, maybe too extreme. Because Eurovision ...

00:01:34.680 --> 00:01:38.980
My opinion is that it's not really about music. You know, it's about the show.

00:01:39.600 --> 00:01:44.660
You know, it's a show to make people enjoy the all the new technology the new

00:01:44.940 --> 00:01:47.020
sound of the things, you know.

00:01:47.020 --> 00:01:51.440
What was the first thought that went through your head when they

00:01:51.520 --> 00:01:55.020
announced you as the winner of the international competition?

00:01:56.060 --> 00:01:58.940
My first thought was «OH MY GOD»!

00:02:00.040 --> 00:02:02.040
But in Portuguese, yeah.

00:02:02.500 --> 00:02:09.340
No, my first thought, you know, we we were far from the stage and the stage had a lot of stairs

00:02:10.780 --> 00:02:14.840
How do you say «stairs»? «Trapper».

00:02:17.920 --> 00:02:25.480
So I was very ill back then and for me, it was very difficult for me to go up stairs.

00:02:26.200 --> 00:02:29.460
So I was really nervous about that. I got super tired.

00:02:29.740 --> 00:02:34.260
So I was like, «oh no, I won and now I'm gonna have to climb all those stairs»!

00:02:35.440 --> 00:02:41.760
That was honestly my first ... I think if you really watched it carefully at that moment

00:02:41.920 --> 00:02:44.760
I think you can tell by my face that I'm like, «oh no»!

00:02:46.180 --> 00:02:47.440
Yeah, I got really tired

00:02:47.440 --> 00:02:50.800
just going up the four stairs, you know. Four stairs!

00:02:51.720 --> 00:02:55.660
I mean, back then you had this serious heart condition.

00:02:55.660 --> 00:02:56.540
Yeah.

00:02:56.860 --> 00:03:01.520
And was this was this the way you could notice that you got

00:03:01.700 --> 00:03:02.660
easily tired?

00:03:03.120 --> 00:03:05.880
If the heart doesn't function, anything else in the body doesn't really function.

00:03:05.880 --> 00:03:10.280
So I got tired, you know, I had a lot of liquid retention also.

00:03:10.820 --> 00:03:14.880
Yeah. A lot of liquid. You know, I had like 25 kilos of

00:03:14.920 --> 00:03:16.180
liquid in my body.

00:03:16.180 --> 00:03:21.960
I had a stomach like this, like an old beer guy.

00:03:22.360 --> 00:03:24.740
Was this during the Eurosong?

00:03:24.940 --> 00:03:30.320
Yeah, I had ... If you look I was wearing a very large shirt, so it you couldn't notice. A black shirt.

00:03:31.549 --> 00:03:36.849
But if you look carefully you can see that there's something there, you know. But now I play football

00:03:37.690 --> 00:03:39.969
two hours a week!

00:03:40.720 --> 00:03:45.860
And I run. I can do anything now!

00:03:49.640 --> 00:03:57.640
The reason that you could, if I understand right here, the reason that you could go through with the whole Eurosong thing

00:03:58.380 --> 00:04:03.540
was ... You owe parts of that to your sister because ...

00:04:03.540 --> 00:04:09.560
Parts of that? Almost all of it! My sister wrote the song.

00:04:09.640 --> 00:04:11.640
Yeah, the song.

00:04:12.319 --> 00:04:16.328
Yeah, she stepped in for me in the rehearsals for a week.

00:04:16.430 --> 00:04:21.489
But was that ... I mean, when you win a victory like that

00:04:22.120 --> 00:04:26.840
It's a whole year that is sort of a bit like being a part of a big circus.

00:04:27.960 --> 00:04:32.580
Was there like a moment when you realizes «I can't be a part of the circus»?

00:04:32.590 --> 00:04:35.320
I can't be ... I'm not fit for this.

00:04:35.349 --> 00:04:42.669
Yeah, that moment happened before because they have ... before Eurovision, as you must know, they have a lot of parties ...

00:04:42.669 --> 00:04:48.489
You know, Eurovision pre-party and I couldn't do it physically, but I didn't want to do it either, you know.

00:04:48.490 --> 00:04:49.840
Because they had it in clubs, you know.

00:04:49.840 --> 00:04:55.840
I don't really like clubs and it's a whole world where there's a lot of things that I just don't identify with.

00:04:55.840 --> 00:05:00.730
You know, so from the beginning I was a bit apart from everything until the end, you know.

00:05:00.800 --> 00:05:05.460
Right after I won there was a lot of things to do like the winners should do

00:05:05.560 --> 00:05:06.680
and

00:05:06.680 --> 00:05:11.320
It's not that I'm against it. It's just that I don't identify with it.

00:05:11.800 --> 00:05:16.200
You had a long period, I don't know how long it was, but you were waiting.

00:05:16.940 --> 00:05:19.360
Six months.

00:05:19.860 --> 00:05:21.360
What were you doing?

00:05:21.480 --> 00:05:25.980
I was waiting. Waiting for a transplant.

00:05:26.140 --> 00:05:28.900
Could you could you write songs? Could you work?

00:05:29.260 --> 00:05:32.060
Are there songs on your album that are from that period?

00:05:32.340 --> 00:05:36.260
It would be very romantic to say that I wrote

00:05:36.400 --> 00:05:40.760
a lot of songs in my very hard period of my life!

00:05:47.420 --> 00:05:52.480
The reality really is that I just watched series on Netflix. I was so depressed, you know.

00:05:53.930 --> 00:05:55.930
Well, I also

00:05:56.330 --> 00:06:02.679
saw a lot of Ingmar Bergman films. Roy Andersson films. «En kärlekshistoria».

00:06:03.680 --> 00:06:06.160
But no, I didn't write songs

00:06:06.160 --> 00:06:10.059
and then after I wrote a couple of songs that that are gonna be in my next album.

00:06:10.100 --> 00:06:14.920
The first song, actually, is really about that experience and it's a sort of a

00:06:15.720 --> 00:06:21.300
look at the catharsis moment and it's actually separated from the rest of the album

00:06:21.310 --> 00:06:27.220
so you have the first song which is like the catharsis of that moment and then afterwards the album really begins and it's like a

00:06:27.940 --> 00:06:30.340
rebirth album, you know.

00:06:30.900 --> 00:06:32.440
And that's where you are now?

00:06:32.440 --> 00:06:34.040
That's where I am now.

00:06:34.040 --> 00:06:37.660
How was it to go on stage for the first time as ...

00:06:38.080 --> 00:06:40.080
With a new heart?

00:06:40.280 --> 00:06:46.270
It's funny that you ask that. The first time I did it in a bar where I play often in Portugal, but

00:06:46.940 --> 00:06:51.160
I didn't have any strength in my legs, you know, because I'd been

00:06:53.480 --> 00:06:56.060
laying down ... How do you say?

00:06:56.060 --> 00:06:57.980
Bedridden.

00:06:57.980 --> 00:07:02.360
That's okay in three weeks, that's not one of the first words you learn anyway!

00:07:02.900 --> 00:07:08.860
Yeah, so had a laid down for so long. I didn't have the muscles, you know. So I remember trying to sing and

00:07:09.650 --> 00:07:14.509
my voice just rambled all over because I don't know why, I didn't have the strength in my voice

00:07:14.510 --> 00:07:15.650
I didn't have the strength anyway

00:07:15.650 --> 00:07:22.850
And I was so frustrated singing a song that I just jumped and did this and I fell on stage, you know.

00:07:22.850 --> 00:07:24.200
I fell on stage!

00:07:24.200 --> 00:07:28.430
It was a bar, you know, but I fell and I'm like «I should leave», you know.

00:07:28.430 --> 00:07:31.880
I was so sad and then little by little

00:07:33.620 --> 00:07:38.120
I began singing

00:07:38.280 --> 00:07:40.200
well. Better.

00:07:40.200 --> 00:07:46.640
And now ... I don't think it's there yet, but it's getting there. The voice, you know.

00:07:46.860 --> 00:07:49.380
But you feel okay?

00:07:49.560 --> 00:07:52.140
Yeah, yeah, yeah! Really well!

00:07:52.260 --> 00:07:54.260
But do you know whose heart you got?

00:07:55.400 --> 00:07:57.320
No, no, no, no!

00:07:57.320 --> 00:08:00.940
That's impossible to know, you know, and I wouldn't wanna know.

00:08:01.760 --> 00:08:04.760
I just feel fine. Who cares whose it is, you know.

00:08:04.760 --> 00:08:07.480
But anyway, it's a great heart, isn't it?

00:08:07.540 --> 00:08:09.800
Yes, yes, yes. Absolutely.

00:08:09.940 --> 00:08:13.420
I'm so amazed that you're here tonight. I'm so glad you're here tonight. And

00:08:13.680 --> 00:08:15.900
we're gonna have some other guests on.

00:08:16.160 --> 00:08:19.200
And later on you're gonna sing for us as well.

00:08:19.700 --> 00:08:20.900
Yeah, yeah, yeah.

00:08:26.780 --> 00:08:31.080
Hope you enjoyed the clip! For more interesting conversations, please hit subscribe.

